From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p: reset input history only on remote restart

Ordinary notifications must retain the last observed entry values. Otherwise
an unrelated entry update replays every asserted rising-edge interrupt,
including ADSP ready and handover. Preserve the v2 restart reset when the
remote restart flag actually differs from the acknowledged flag.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -199,5 +199,8 @@
 	restart_done = in->flags & BIT(SMP2P_FLAGS_RESTART_DONE_BIT);
 	restart = restart_done != smp2p->ssr_ack;
+	if (!restart)
+		return false;
+
 	list_for_each_entry(entry, &smp2p->inbound, node) {
 		if (!entry->value)
 			continue;
